Id: no-unescaped-render-in-config-page
Pattern: (\.innerHTML|\.outerHTML|document\.write|insertAdjacentHTML)
Subject: *.html
Except: none
Issue: 43

The configuration page is HTML with script in it, rendered in an administrator's
browser, and the values it draws come from a configuration document and, once
#74 lands, from a third party's response. Writing any of that into the page as
markup rather than as text is how a response becomes script in the one browser
session that can change every setting this plugin has.

The refused calls are the ones that treat a string as markup. Setting text is
not refused, and it is the replacement.
